@page "/kilder"
@using ModernHost.Components

<PageTitle>Modern host — kilder</PageTitle>

<div class="hostchrome">
    <p class="hostchrome-note">
        The other root component the package ships: <code>KildeExplorer</code>, the
        kildeutforsker. <code>VariableSearch</code> is on <a href="/">the front page</a> — the
        two are separate entry points, not two tabs of one thing, so each gets a page here.
    </p>
    <p class="hostchrome-note">
        <strong>The component is behind a wrapper here, not mounted straight onto the tag</strong>,
        and that is forced rather than chosen. <code>KildeExplorer</code> raises
        <code>ExploreVariablesRequested</code>, and an <code>EventCallback</code> does not survive
        being passed from a statically-rendered parent into an interactive island: it is
        serialised as <code>{"HasDelegate":true}</code> and read back as an empty delegate, so the
        handler never runs. <code>@@rendermode</code> on the component tag does not fix that — it
        makes the mount point interactive while the parent creating the callback stays static.
        The callback has to be created <em>inside</em> the interactive component, so the wrapper
        is the island. <a href="/">The front page</a> mounts straight onto the tag and is right
        to: it passes only data, and data crosses the boundary intact.
    </p>
    <p class="hostchrome-note">
        <code>prerender: false</code> is separate, and not a preference either:
        <code>KildeExplorer</code> fetches the whole kilde list when it initialises, and
        prerendering would run that call twice against the API on every page load.
    </p>
</div>

<div class="hostframe">
    @* render-mode is set HERE, by the host, on the wrapper that owns the handover — see the note
       above for why it cannot go on the KildeExplorer tag inside it. The package's own components
       stay render-mode free either way, which is the rule that lets them mount in LegacyHost's
       MVC view too. *@
    <KildeExplorerWithHandover Language="no"
                               @rendermode="@(new InteractiveServerRenderMode(prerender: false))" />
</div>
